(2171151, 298832, 47117, '<td valign="top">When using a real full model shot for fashion photography, one has to be very careful how and what is being portrayed.  This comes down to many factors, but mainly the model herself can make or break the ad, the product, the shot, etc. This would have been a fantastic shot if it weren''t for a few obvious flaws. The model herself is just gorgeous.  VERY expressive eyes, gorgeous hair flow, nice scenery, well fitting clothes.  Here are the obvious flaws. It looks like some army officer was yelling at her to stand up straight and stick out her chest. She is WAY too straight. A totally unnatural pose, and looks like she is purposely sticking out her chest, if not subconciously.  Her face alone would have made this shot perfect, with background as is and just cropped, but her pose ruins it. The hat just hanging straight down like that speaks nothing for the fashion.  It''s really a pity, and I would actually reshoot this and place it in a portfolio for her in which she should use for actual modeling, but after some lessons. This shot had a HUGE amount of potential, and if modeled correctly can make a wonderful portfolio shot. Still scored it high, for potential, for beauty of the model, and for scenery.</td>', 'When using a real full model shot for fashion photography, one has to be very careful how and what is being portrayed.  This comes down to many factors, but mainly the model herself can make or break the ad, the product, the shot, etc. This would have been a fantastic shot if it weren''t for a few obvious flaws. The model herself is just gorgeous.  VERY expressive eyes, gorgeous hair flow, nice scenery, well fitting clothes.  Here are the obvious flaws. It looks like some army officer was yelling at her to stand up straight and stick out her chest. She is WAY too straight. A totally unnatural pose, and looks like she is purposely sticking out her chest, if not subconciously.  Her face alone would have made this shot perfect, with background as is and just cropped, but her pose ruins it. The hat just hanging straight down like that speaks nothing for the fashion.  It''s really a pity, and I would actually reshoot this and place it in a portfolio for her in which she should use for actual modeling, but after some lessons. This shot had a HUGE amount of potential, and if modeled correctly can make a wonderful portfolio shot. Still scored it high, for potential, for beauty of the model, and for scenery.', '2006-02-22 10:29:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2171161, 298535, 39988, '<td valign="top">The hat sets this photo off along with this attractive woman, very nice meeting challenge and pic</td>', 'The hat sets this photo off along with this attractive woman, very nice meeting challenge and pic', '2006-02-22 10:30:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2171191, 297445, 21216, '<td valign="top">Now this is fashion. <br/> <br/>This is a ribbon ;)</td>', 'Now this is fashion.  This is a ribbon ;)', '2006-02-22 10:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2171202, 296491, 47117, '<td valign="top">When using a real live full photo model in fashion photography, it is a very risky thing to do for ads, fashion, etc. This is why it is so much hard work to be a model. They have to portray the product or fashion in the proper way. However, on the risk you took in using a model in this way, here is my critique.  I first want to comment on the title, "Curves". I believe it is actually the name of a product. I believe a perfume. I would have had that in the shot and her holding it. I know this wasn''t a challenge for ads, but the dress alone really is just a dress and doesn''t do much for me.  The hip action is also a bit too severe. Almost in a distracting way. With the product it would have made more sense, but without it, it seems an un-necessary stance. This model is very pretty and the huge swing in the hip is just overpowering her and drawing the eye to the hip. It also draws the eye to the bracelettes, which don''t work with this gown. On the other hand, from the chest up, her facial expression is spot on and she is showing a nice amount of neck for the stance, but that hip, again, pulling it out so far has hunched her shoulders, taking away from the potential this shot could have had.  In any case, it is still pleasing. I like the soft focus, and the red on black, etc. I still gave it a decent score.</td>', 'When using a real live full photo model in fashion photography, it is a very risky thing to do for ads, fashion, etc. This is why it is so much hard work to be a model. They have to portray the product or fashion in the proper way. However, on the risk you took in using a model in this way, here is my critique.  I first want to comment on the title, "Curves". I believe it is actually the name of a product. I believe a perfume. I would have had that in the shot and her holding it. I know this wasn''t a challenge for ads, but the dress alone really is just a dress and doesn''t do much for me.  The hip action is also a bit too severe. Almost in a distracting way. With the product it would have made more sense, but without it, it seems an un-necessary stance. This model is very pretty and the huge swing in the hip is just overpowering her and drawing the eye to the hip. It also draws the eye to the bracelettes, which don''t work with this gown. On the other hand, from the chest up, her facial expression is spot on and she is showing a nice amount of neck for the stance, but that hip, again, pulling it out so far has hunched her shoulders, taking away from the potential this shot could have had.  In any case, it is still pleasing. I like the soft focus, and the red on black, etc. I still gave it a decent score.', '2006-02-22 10:37:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2171217, 298972, 47117, '<td valign="top">This model has very good facial features and structure in jaw line and eye expression. Very balanced features. I also love the pose. Make up is an issue though. Unfortunately, her face make up seems to enhance the flaws rather than mask them. The lines under the eyes and on the forehead needed to be masked with make up for this type of shot, which I believe is a make up fashion shot. Other than that, a very pleasing photo.</td>', 'This model has very good facial features and structure in jaw line and eye expression. Very balanced features. I also love the pose. Make up is an issue though. Unfortunately, her face make up seems to enhance the flaws rather than mask them. The lines under the eyes and on the forehead needed to be masked with make up for this type of shot, which I believe is a make up fashion shot. Other than that, a very pleasing photo.', '2006-02-22 10:40:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2171231, 296650, 46428, '<td valign="top">Very nice. Would have been much much better if the nipple was completely hidden ;-) 8.</td>', 'Very nice. Would have been much much better if the nipple was completely hidden ;-) 8.', '2006-02-22 10:43:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2171268, 298844, 46428, '<td valign="top">Cute.. 7.</td>', 'Cute.. 7.', '2006-02-22 10:50:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2171279, 296650, 47117, '<td valign="top">THIS is a problem. LOL...Ok, I see the idea here was to model longerie. Sorry, I am not up on how to spell that, so for this critique I will just say sexy wear.  In using a real live actual model for this shot, it is a risky venture.  The model and the clothes all have to balance each other out in order to sell the photo.  Speaking on the model''s stance alone, the pose is very good. A flaw in most model shots though is that they tend to look more porn in expression then alluring when the the mouth is open just a tad.  A closed mouth in this shot would have worked better. The eye make up is also to severe. Less is more in this type of shot and with beautiful blue eyes.  She does show a nice amount of neck though, which is difficult to do with this pose.  As for the outfit itself, WHO is going to look at it when a nipple is showing? LOL...In real fashion photography this would have been retouched not to show. For basic editing, I would have reshot this and taped her bossum down if needed in that area so she could still make this pose and have the garment look as it if fits properly.  It''s the mystery of this type of fashion style that sells or is more pleasing then when that mystery is taken away. It almost is as if the outfit doesn''t fit her correctly, or this was done for <i>Playboy</i> rather than <i>Victoria Secret</i>. I would have preferred the Victoria Secret route myself. Other than that, the background is nice and has little noise or distraction to the model, and the colors on this model are nice. Blue rather than red would have been a better choice though. Her eyes would have really popped.  But that make up and the nipple just really distract. I still gave it a decent score for the potential it could have had.</td>', 'THIS is a problem. LOL...Ok, I see the idea here was to model longerie. Sorry, I am not up on how to spell that, so for this critique I will just say sexy wear.  In using a real live actual model for this shot, it is a risky venture.  The model and the clothes all have to balance each other out in order to sell the photo.  Speaking on the model''s stance alone, the pose is very good. A flaw in most model shots though is that they tend to look more porn in expression then alluring when the the mouth is open just a tad.  A closed mouth in this shot would have worked better. The eye make up is also to severe. Less is more in this type of shot and with beautiful blue eyes.  She does show a nice amount of neck though, which is difficult to do with this pose.  As for the outfit itself, WHO is going to look at it when a nipple is showing? LOL...In real fashion photography this would have been retouched not to show. For basic editing, I would have reshot this and taped her bossum down if needed in that area so she could still make this pose and have the garment look as it if fits properly.  It''s the mystery of this type of fashion style that sells or is more pleasing then when that mystery is taken away. It almost is as if the outfit doesn''t fit her correctly, or this was done for Playboy rather than Victoria Secret. I would have preferred the Victoria Secret route myself. Other than that, the background is nice and has little noise or distraction to the model, and the colors on this model are nice. Blue rather than red would have been a better choice though. Her eyes would have really popped.  But that make up and the nipple just really distract. I still gave it a decent score for the potential it could have had.', '2006-02-22 10:51:56.000000', NULL, 1),
