(2179667, 296650, 19672, '<td valign="top">Very nice, great colors. Beautiful model and outfit. But something doesn''t quite jibe with me right.<br/> <br/>I think it''s two factors. <br/>a) Hide areola. She''s extremely well endowed but it almost becomes a distracting element. Minimize them being the biggest draw. Sure, present them...but present her as a whole.<br/> <br/>b)something is slightly off for me regarding the face and lips. I am pin-pointing it down to a little ridge on the upper noise. It distracts from the perfection of her face. Not really a flaw but it creates a slightly off angle.  I think her lips being in a narrow pursed position make for a thin feel to her feature but her face is not narrow. Makes me feel like something is off on the perspective. . You can see a slight line from the nose to the lips. Furthers this narrow facial feature feel. (Not sure if you can see what I am describing.) It''s very very minor. But it makes me notice it all.  I think a little PS editing can compensate.  Also, I don''t like the lavender makeup under her eyebrows. It adds a color only seen there and it clashes with the rest of the chosen color palette.<br/> <br/>That said, excellent take. I was very critical but it''s because you''re shot is quite up there and needs the very finest detail to push your photography to that pinnacle. <br/> <br/>;) <br/> <br/>(8)</td>', 'Very nice, great colors. Beautiful model and outfit. But something doesn''t quite jibe with me right. I think it''s two factors. a) Hide areola. She''s extremely well endowed but it almost becomes a distracting element. Minimize them being the biggest draw. Sure, present them...but present her as a whole. b)something is slightly off for me regarding the face and lips. I am pin-pointing it down to a little ridge on the upper noise. It distracts from the perfection of her face. Not really a flaw but it creates a slightly off angle.  I think her lips being in a narrow pursed position make for a thin feel to her feature but her face is not narrow. Makes me feel like something is off on the perspective. . You can see a slight line from the nose to the lips. Furthers this narrow facial feature feel. (Not sure if you can see what I am describing.) It''s very very minor. But it makes me notice it all.  I think a little PS editing can compensate.  Also, I don''t like the lavender makeup under her eyebrows. It adds a color only seen there and it clashes with the rest of the chosen color palette. That said, excellent take. I was very critical but it''s because you''re shot is quite up there and needs the very finest detail to push your photography to that pinnacle.  ;)  (8)', '2006-02-24 14:17:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2179979, 298888, 35645, '<td valign="top">This is a very interesting abstract image. For me, however, it has only a tenuous hold on the ''fashion'' aspect of the challenge. Does it meet the challenge, IMO? Yes, barely. Do I like it? Yes. Does it say to me ''I''m a fashion photo''? No.<br/>Also, there appears to be a slight amout of ''bleedover'' between the white and black in some areas.</td>', 'This is a very interesting abstract image. For me, however, it has only a tenuous hold on the ''fashion'' aspect of the challenge. Does it meet the challenge, IMO? Yes, barely. Do I like it? Yes. Does it say to me ''I''m a fashion photo''? No.Also, there appears to be a slight amout of ''bleedover'' between the white and black in some areas.', '2006-02-24 16:16:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2179991, 298034, 35645, '<td valign="top">I really don''t like the background in this photo. And there''s a lot going on in the immediate foreground that seems unnecessary. I think that if these items were arranged a little differently in front of a new background, this photo would be much more pleaseing to the eye. As it stands now, it really just looks like a bunch of ''stuff'' thrown at the mannequin - there is no order to it, no sequence for the eye to follow. And the background just clashes with everything else.</td>', 'I really don''t like the background in this photo. And there''s a lot going on in the immediate foreground that seems unnecessary. I think that if these items were arranged a little differently in front of a new background, this photo would be much more pleaseing to the eye. As it stands now, it really just looks like a bunch of ''stuff'' thrown at the mannequin - there is no order to it, no sequence for the eye to follow. And the background just clashes with everything else.', '2006-02-24 16:20:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2179997, 296104, 35645, '<td valign="top">I don''t really care for the post processing done to this photo. It''s simply not very flattering to the model. The pose isn''t particularly flattering, either.</td>', 'I don''t really care for the post processing done to this photo. It''s simply not very flattering to the model. The pose isn''t particularly flattering, either.', '2006-02-24 16:21:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2180002, 298834, 35645, '<td valign="top">Hmm. Very dark photo - except for the lighting glare. Also somewhat out of focus. This perhaps would have turned out better had the bottle been in front of a lighter colored background and if the light were behind a baffle or screen.</td>', 'Hmm. Very dark photo - except for the lighting glare. Also somewhat out of focus. This perhaps would have turned out better had the bottle been in front of a lighter colored background and if the light were behind a baffle or screen.', '2006-02-24 16:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2180019, 298512, 35645, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure that this meets the ''spirit'' of the challenge, but since it technically does, I''ll let that pass without marking off for it. However, if I were a fashion magazine editor, I would have to take a ''pass'' on using this photo for a couple of reasons. 1- While close-ups or macros do indeed appear in some designer ads, they are always crisp and clear throughout the entire picture. 2 - When these close-ups appear, they are usually shown ''in context'' (a cuff on a model''s arm, for example). 3 - The composition is visually boring. There is nothing that leads the eye from one spot to another in the photo; the eye simply jumps around trying to make sense of it. <br/>Also, I don''t know if this is the actual color of the item. It _looks_ like it was added in post processing. So, again, if the color was added after the fact, this would be another cause to not use the photo.<br/>I know that this isn''t a very positive critique, but I hope at least some of it will be helpful to you.</td>', 'I''m not sure that this meets the ''spirit'' of the challenge, but since it technically does, I''ll let that pass without marking off for it. However, if I were a fashion magazine editor, I would have to take a ''pass'' on using this photo for a couple of reasons. 1- While close-ups or macros do indeed appear in some designer ads, they are always crisp and clear throughout the entire picture. 2 - When these close-ups appear, they are usually shown ''in context'' (a cuff on a model''s arm, for example). 3 - The composition is visually boring. There is nothing that leads the eye from one spot to another in the photo; the eye simply jumps around trying to make sense of it. Also, I don''t know if this is the actual color of the item. It _looks_ like it was added in post processing. So, again, if the color was added after the fact, this would be another cause to not use the photo.I know that this isn''t a very positive critique, but I hope at least some of it will be helpful to you.', '2006-02-24 16:29:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2180024, 297823, 35645, '<td valign="top">This would be a more aesthetically pleasing photo if _either_ you lined up the shoes with the lines on the floor _or_ you laid them out so that it looks as though you _deliberately_ did not line them up. This looks like they were tossed out there and photo''d at the last minute. Also, you have a lot of glare from your lighting (flash?) and it looks like you played with the color and saturation a little too much - or perhaps not enough! Another angle might have made this a little more visually appealing - they look a little like they''re in a police line-up at the moment. Not a very positive critique, I know, but hopefully I''ve given you some things to think about and maybe try the next time you shoot something like this.</td>', 'This would be a more aesthetically pleasing photo if _either_ you lined up the shoes with the lines on the floor _or_ you laid them out so that it looks as though you _deliberately_ did not line them up. This looks like they were tossed out there and photo''d at the last minute. Also, you have a lot of glare from your lighting (flash?) and it looks like you played with the color and saturation a little too much - or perhaps not enough! Another angle might have made this a little more visually appealing - they look a little like they''re in a police line-up at the moment. Not a very positive critique, I know, but hopefully I''ve given you some things to think about and maybe try the next time you shoot something like this.', '2006-02-24 16:33:53.000000', NULL, 1),
