(2193819, 297843, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hiya Nick! I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful ;) <br/> <br/>First off I believe that for a "Fashion" challenge, her clothing is quite plain. In as much as black is in, it doesn''t have the same charisma as the other "colorful" images. The lighting is good with no harsh shadows nor hotspots. The focus seems a bit soft though. The way her hands are cut off is a bit distracting. maybe had her hands been on her waist striking the "pose", I think this would be better.<br/> <br/>The other thing that would make this image effective as well is accessories. Fashion is almost always over the top. Don''t you think?<br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'Hiya Nick! I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful ;)  First off I believe that for a "Fashion" challenge, her clothing is quite plain. In as much as black is in, it doesn''t have the same charisma as the other "colorful" images. The lighting is good with no harsh shadows nor hotspots. The focus seems a bit soft though. The way her hands are cut off is a bit distracting. maybe had her hands been on her waist striking the "pose", I think this would be better. The other thing that would make this image effective as well is accessories. Fashion is almost always over the top. Don''t you think? Cheers,  Rikki', '2006-03-01 15:56:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193866, 297843, 40718, '<td valign="top">I gave this shot a 7.  I think it looks pretty good for fashion.  The stark background works because we are supposed to be concentrating on the model and her clothes.  She is appropriately pretty, which is important (unfortunately).  The composition and pose are excellent too.  A 7 from me is a significant score.  What kept it from a higher score was the perceived softness of her hair (see the upper right where the background seems to "invade" the detail of her hair).  I also didn''t like the large black area of no detail where her hair blends with her blouse.  Finally, I would have ditched the earring.  That''s small though.</td>', 'I gave this shot a 7.  I think it looks pretty good for fashion.  The stark background works because we are supposed to be concentrating on the model and her clothes.  She is appropriately pretty, which is important (unfortunately).  The composition and pose are excellent too.  A 7 from me is a significant score.  What kept it from a higher score was the perceived softness of her hair (see the upper right where the background seems to "invade" the detail of her hair).  I also didn''t like the large black area of no detail where her hair blends with her blouse.  Finally, I would have ditched the earring.  That''s small though.', '2006-03-01 16:18:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193914, 298832, 10768, '<td valign="top">Yea!  My highest finish - a top 10!  I drifted away from DPC for a while, but I have always visited the site to view the photos.  I missed having a designated photo challenge though.  I decided to up my participation and do the Fashion challenge.  I originally planned on more of a studio shot.  My in-laws were visiting though and I didn''t want to turn my living room upside-down to take pictures.  I waited until the day of the contest and drug my daughter out to one of my favorite photo spots.  It was close to sundown and the lighting was really good.  I only did some minor level adjustments, sharpening and I ran it through Neat Image.  This has really motivated me to take more photos and to enter more often.  Thanks to all who have commented.  I''ve learned something from each of your remarks.</td>', 'Yea!  My highest finish - a top 10!  I drifted away from DPC for a while, but I have always visited the site to view the photos.  I missed having a designated photo challenge though.  I decided to up my participation and do the Fashion challenge.  I originally planned on more of a studio shot.  My in-laws were visiting though and I didn''t want to turn my living room upside-down to take pictures.  I waited until the day of the contest and drug my daughter out to one of my favorite photo spots.  It was close to sundown and the lighting was really good.  I only did some minor level adjustments, sharpening and I ran it through Neat Image.  This has really motivated me to take more photos and to enter more often.  Thanks to all who have commented.  I''ve learned something from each of your remarks.', '2006-03-01 16:34:49.000000', NULL, 0),
